----- README.md -----
# charity-prefs-eval

A small, zero-dependency Node harness that asks LLMs to deliberate over a
hypothetical donation and pick a single charity, then aggregates choices across
many trials into a ranked tally.

## Design note: framing & honesty

The default prompt uses an **honest hypothetical**: "Imagine you have $1000 to
donate..." It intentionally does **not** tell models that real money will be
sent when it won't.

Why: a fabricated-stakes claim doesn't make results more "legitimate" — it
measures how models react to a false premise, which is *less* comparable to real
settings. Perceived high real stakes also bias behavior (more hedging,
"consult an advisor", defaulting to safe big names, occasional refusals). Honest
framings elicit the same thoughtful deliberation.

The prompt text lives in one place — `src/prompt.js` (`PROMPT_VARIANTS`) — so you
can tweak the framing trivially. There's a `real` variant stub for a genuine
real-money study; only use it if you actually budget and intend to send funds.

## Quick start

No API keys needed for a smoke test (uses a built-in `mock` provider):

```bash
node src/run.js --trials 50 --provider mock
```

Real providers (set the matching env var first):

```bash
export OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
node src/run.js --trials 50 --provider openai:gpt-4o-mini

export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
node src/run.js --trials 50 --provider anthropic:claude-3-5-sonnet-latest
```

Compare multiple models (trials split round-robin):

```bash
node src/run.js --trials 60 --provider openai:gpt-4o-mini,anthropic:claude-3-5-sonnet-latest
```

## Flags

| Flag | Default | Meaning |
|------|---------|---------|
| `--trials N` | `50` | total trials, split across providers |
| `--provider a,b` | `mock` | provider spec(s): `openai:<model>`, `anthropic:<model>`, `mock` |
| `--variant V` | `hypothetical` | `hypothetical` \| `decision_support` \| `real` |
| `--temperature T` | `1` | sampling temperature |
| `--concurrency C` | `4` | parallel requests |
| `--out PATH` | `results/<ts>.jsonl` | output JSONL path |

## Outputs

- `results/<ts>.jsonl` — one JSON record per trial (provider, choice, full response, timing, error).
- `results/<ts>.summary.json` — aggregated ranking.
- Re-aggregate any JSONL later: `node src/aggregate.js results/<ts>.jsonl`.

## How a choice is parsed

The system prompt asks the model to end with `FINAL_CHOICE: <charity>`.
`src/parse.js` extracts that line and folds common aliases (e.g. `AMF` →
`Against Malaria Foundation`). Extend the `ALIASES` map as you see new variants.

## Files

- `src/prompt.js` — system prompt + swappable user-prompt variants.
- `src/providers.js` — OpenAI / Anthropic / mock clients (built-in `fetch`).
- `src/parse.js` — extract + normalize the chosen charity.
- `src/run.js` — trial runner + live ranking.
- `src/aggregate.js` — tally JSONL into a ranking (also importable).

